(56, 'en', 'help_search', ' creating a comment type goal create a new comment type see managing comments for information about comments and comment types who can create a comment type  users with the administer comment types and settings permission typically administrators can create comment types steps in the manage administrative menu navigate to structure   comment types  click add comment type  in the label field enter a name for the comment type which is how it will be listed in the administrative interface in the target entity type field select the entity type to be commented on see managing content structure for more about content entities and fields click save  the comment type will be created optionally if you have the core field ui module installed you can follow the steps in the related topics to add fields to the new comment type set up the editing form and configure the display  ', 0),
(56, 'en', 'node_search', ' daksh daksh vision central public sector enterprises cpses are pivotal to india s socioeconomic growth contributing significantly to industrial development employment innovation and more than 13 of the national gdp as india advances toward its vision of viksit bharat 2047  the leadership of cpses must be futureready to navigate complex challenges and global opportunities daksh developed by the capacity building commission cbc in collaboration with the standing conference of public enterprises scope is envisioned as a flagship common leadership development programme cldp for senior executives of cpses it is designed to build a sustained pipeline of leaders capable of assuming boardlevel responsibilities thereby institutionalising leadership succession in the public sector the vision of daksh is to create a pool of strategic ethical and globally competent leaders who can drive cpses to higher levels of performance and governance excellence the program integrates structured learning international exposure live projects coaching and immersive experiences to develop leaders holistically enhancing their strategic foresight technological adaptability resilience and ability to lead diverse teams in an increasingly interconnected world daksh aims not only to address immediate leadership needs but also to embed a culture of continuous capacitybuilding within cpses over the upcoming years the programme will equip  2000 senior executives  gms cgms eds or equivalent with competencies to take on board positions thus ensuring that leadership transitions in cpses are robust and futureready objective develop leadership competencies among senior executives gms cgms eds to prepare them for boardlevel roles institutionalise a structured selection and assessment process including psychometric tests individual development plans idps and coaching provide exposure to contemporary global practices through international immersion thoughtleadership seminars and industry visits facilitate crosslearning among cpses through a common platform building an alumni network of senior leaders build a sustained talent pool of 2000 futureready leaders across cpses in the upcoming years institutionalise succession planning in cpses by ensuring a steady supply of ready now soon and later leaders enhance organizational agility and competitiveness of cpses by equipping leaders with skills in strategy finance technology and change management conseptual framework program overview daksh is a 12month leadership programme that combines classroom learning online modules international exposure spiritual and outbound training live action learning projects and oneonone coaching each cohort comprises 6080 participants  carefully selected based on a specified eligibility criteria the programme journey includes  assessment idps for comprehensive diagnostics to design personalised learning paths  immersions including domestic and international industry visits eg alpine university in austria unternehmertum in munich red bull hq in salzburg  live action learning projects with group projects linked to strategic challenges of cpses  leadership immersion workshops thought leadership seminars with global experts industry leaders and academic partners and spiritual outbound training for building resilience collaboration and mindfulness the first batch launched in april 2025 with mckinsey as knowledge partner and iim ahmedabad as academic partner based on future cohorts will be facilitated by egon zehnder with iim indore and isb daksh s longterm ambition is to build a pool of  2000 futureready cpse leaders in the upcoming years institutionalising succession planning and creating a robust pool of leaders ready to take on boardlevel responsibilities assessment idps comprehensive diagnostics to design personalised learning paths international immersions domestic and international industry visits to global institutions live action learning group projects linked to strategic challenges of cpses coaching workshops oneonone coaching and thought leadership seminars chronology of events   august 2024 concept note finalised after consultations with cpses rbi fsib and expert panels  january 2025 daksh brochure released  april 2025 batch 1 launched knowledge partner mckinsey academic partner iim ahmedabad  june 2025 mou signed with egon zehnder as the knowledge partner and iim indore as an academic partner for batch 2  july 2025 classroom immersion initiated for batch 1 at iim ahmedabad  august 2025 international immersion in austria germany alpine university unternehmertum red bull hq for batch 1  september 2025 spiritual outbound training for batch 1  2026 onwards scaling up with multiple cohorts annually egon zehnder with iim indore isb empanelled for upcoming batches key milestones launch of daksh batch 1 april 2025 classroom immersion at iim ahmedabad july 2025 international immersion august 2025 spiritual outbound training september 2025 target 2000 cpse leaders upcoming cohorts mou with egon zehnder iim indore june 2025 batch 2 relevant data 73 participants enrolled in batch 1 impact metrics participant engagement 100  of surveyed participants recommend the program to peers engagement score  465  programme design rating  465 skill development participants reported enhanced global outlook   inclusive leadership skills  and resilience  way forward scaling strategy next steps train  2000 senior executives  gms cgms eds across cpses over the upcoming years multiple cohorts annually with academic partners  iim ahmedabad iim indore isb  and knowledge partners  mckinsey egon zehnder   continuous improvement through impact assessments participant feedback and steering committee oversight integration with national capacity building plan positioning daksh as a flagship leadership programme for cpses under mission karmayogi strengthening alumni networks across cpses to promote sustained peer learning and crosssector collaboration academic partners iim ahmedabad iim indore isb knowledge partners mckinsey egon zehnder admin fri 12 dec 2025 554  ', 0),
(56, 'hi', 'help_search', ' creating a comment type लक्ष्य create a new comment type see managing comments for information about comments and comment types who can create a comment type  users with the administer comment types and settings permission typically administrators can create comment types steps in the manage administrative menu navigate to structure   comment types  click add comment type  in the label field enter a name for the comment type which is how it will be listed in the administrative interface in the target entity type field select the entity type to be commented on see managing content structure for more about content entities and fields click save  the comment type will be created optionally if you have the core field ui module installed you can follow the steps in the related topics to add fields to the new comment type set up the editing form and configure the display  ', 0),
(57, 'en', 'help_search', ' disabling comments goal turn off commenting for a particular entity see managing content structure for more about content entities and fields note that if you want to turn off commenting for all entities of an entity type or subtype you will need to edit the field settings for the comment field see configuring comments for more about configuring the comment field who can disable comments  you will need the administer comments and comment settings permission in order to disable commenting you will also need permission to edit the entity that the comments are on steps find the entity you want to disable comments for and edit it for example to turn off comments on a content item you could find it by navigating in the manage administrative menu to content  filtering to find the content item and clicking edit  under comment settings  select the desired comment setting  open  comments are allowed closed  past comments remain visible but no new comments are allowed hidden  past comments are hidden and no new comments are allowed save the entity  ', 0),
(57, 'en', 'node_search', ' faculty development programs faculty development programs vision of capacity building commission capacity building commission cbc was constituted in april 2021 under mission karmayogi national program for civil services capacity building npcscb mission karmayogi is a government of india initiative that aims to transform capacity building efforts across different levels of government to improve the execution capacity of civil servants and foster citizencentricity cbc wishes to strengthen the capacity of civil service training institutes across the country central government overlooks around 1100 training institutes including 25 central training institutes ctis and 33 state administrative training institutes atis the faculty at these training institutes forms the anchor for success of training of public service officials faculty development program ideation capacity building commission under its efforts for building state capacity wishes to train all the faculty in civil service training institutes by march 2024 the faculty in these cstis have a rich field experience which is highly relevant to train officers for ensuring high performance and better delivery of public service these faculty lack the scientific acumen of teaching effectively this hypothesis is validated by roundtable discussion with faculties as well as a pilot program and its evaluation facilitated by cbc to ensure the fulfilment of this crucial gap cbc has planned a twophase intervention to build capacity of faculties across cstis 60 percent of the faculty in cstis should be civil service practitioners who bring the richness of their experience to their training in the training institutes the practitioner s experiences backed by academic theories and frameworks can form the foundation for enhancing the capacity of the learners by training the cstis faculty they will be encouraged to  utilise their experiences in civil services in the shadow of academic theory to bring the attention of their learners towards impact and achieving positive outcomes in their service towards the nation and its citizens approach training at their cstis with a facilitative approach to motivate their learners for utilizing opportunities of upgrading their skills and adapt a citizencentric service delivery mindset conduct training based on adult learning and learning design principles to place the context of their learning which is most relatable to their learners run training programs that rely on reflection feedback on practice and peerdriven processes for enhancing learning and cocreating contextual learning content build a body of knowledge and best practices to highlight achievements of indian public administration as well as promote these practices for global learning the twophase intervention through the planned twophase intervention cbc wishes to build an internal capacity within the government ecosystem for faculty development the master trainers trained in level 2 of the faculty development program as mentioned below will create a diverse pool of master trainers who will continue to be trainers on faculty development and can be utilised by any civil service training institute phase 1 mandatory online selfpaced training duration  68 hours this online training on igot platform will cover the theoretical aspects to understand the process of learning and teaching in a scientific manner this level1 training program will cover associated theories and principles that help design and deliver an effective training program as well as help appreciate the process of change through a teaching intervention this training program is a mandatory undertaking for any faculty being posted to a csti irrespective of the nature and duration of their tenure completion and performance on this program will be certified by capacity building commission phase 2 advanced faculty development programs target  100150 selected faculty members cbc will host advanced faculty development programs for selected 100150 faculty members from across the cstis the csti heads nominating faculty for these programs will make sure that the participant is a senior faculty who will continue to stay in the training ecosystem for at least another year and will create a corresponding impact in their own institute further these faculty will be listed as master trainers by cbc and will continue to train the faculty from other institutes the faculty development programs planned for the selected cohort are as below  level2 programs for upto 40 participants  sno level2 programs for upto 40 participants  number of batches 1 teaching effectiveness 3 batches 2 training impact assessment 1 batch 3 technologyenabled learning 1 batch pilot faculty development programs facilitated by cbc pilot faculty development program for a homogeneous mixture of 40 officers from national academy of customs indirect taxes and narcotics nacin  the pilot faculty development program for nacin officers conducted by sp jain institute of management and research spjimr and facilitated by capacity building commission was conducted in june 2023 at nacin s campus in bangalore the program covered the theories of teaching effectiveness as well as elements of course design this program based on the intended program objectives and utilized learning design was piloted as a level 1 program this program also helped assess actual gaps in teaching and learning sciences in a csti faculty a pre and postassessment of the associated factors of teaching effectiveness were done for the participants out of 40 participants 32 of them selfassessed themselves on both pre and poststage whose responses have been analysed for the below inferences pre and postassessment analysis on factors of teaching effectiveness in a selfassessment done by the participants they were asked to record their confidence levels in utilizing the belowmentioned techniques and attitudes in their role as a faculty the responses were scored on a scale of  to 5 with 5 representing the highest confidence sno parameter preassessment score  average on a scale of 5  postassessment score  average on a scale of 5  1 practising adult learning principles 13 41 2 utilizing learning facilitation 20 44 3 utilizing learning design principles 28 41 4 facilitating reflective learning 29 41 5 encouraging immersive learning experiences 21 39 6 cocreating content 25 38 7 enabling coaching and feedback 31 44 8 ensuring longterm training impact 32 41 9 building futuristic capabilities 36 43 10 developing digital comfort 36 42 11 transacting field experiences through academic frameworks 19 32 12 measuring impact 28 39 13 staying true to the role of a trainer in the face of challenges 36 43 overall average 273 407 the score on a scale of 5 in the table above represents the average of confidence level scored to their corresponding responses the options and corresponding responses can be referred to in the preassessment questions attached in annexure 1 highlights of the assessment  a  the program recorded an overall delta of 135 on a 5point scale this can be read as an immediate delta or the cognitive gain from the program b  9 out of 13 parameters recorded a delta of more than 1 c  practising adult learning principles utilizing learning facilitation and encouraging immersive experiences recorded the topmost change in terms of confidence in utilizing them the respective values of change on a 5point scale are 28 24 and 18  d  high confidence level for using learning design principles score 4 or above was recorded by 42  of participants before the program and 75  of participants immediately after the program thus transitioning 33  of participants to higher confidence levels the above analysis highlights the important and urgent need to address the cognitive gap in teaching principles and methodologies to capture the scale ie large number of faculty across the civil service training institutions cbc will utilise the program design of the pilot fdp at nacin and transform it into an effective online program this program will be mandatory for all the faculty the elements of program design to be incorporated into the online program have been mentioned in the above section pilot faculty development program facilitated by cbc for a heterogeneous mixture of 27 officers conducted by indian school of business isb  the pilot faculty development program conducted at yashada pune in the month of august invited a heterogeneous mixture of senior faculty from ctis central training institutes and atis administrative training institutes across the country faculty from a total of 14 institutes participated and fulfilled the below criteria the criteria for nomination ensured to invite those faculty who would create maximum impact back at their institutes post the workshop the criteria for nomination  officers who have completed 5 to 7 years of service and are passionate about being a faculty at the academy and officers who have spent at least 1 year at the academy in faculty roles and who have 1 year ahead of them at the institute  the following 14 institutes participated in the faculty development program  bprd central detective training institute hyderabad bprd central detective training institute chandigarh bprd central detective training institute jaipur bprd central detective training institute kolkata national academy of direct taxes nagpur national academy of customs indirect taxes narcotics meghalaya administrative training institute shillong indira gandhi national forest academy dehradun national academy of indian railways nair vadodara institute of government accounts finance delhi rafi ahmed kidwai national postal academy ghaziabad sardar vallabhbhai patel national police academy hyderabad yashwantrao chavan academy of development administration yashada pune kerala institute of local governance cochin the faculty development program conducted by isb was intended as a pilot level 2 program or an advanced program the program focused on two main themes of megatrends in education and how technology is changing the space of education the program relied on the participation of the learners through discussions group work on case discussions and simulations the participants expressed that the program contributed in enhancing their skills as a faculty and rated the program at an average of 467 out of 5  learnings from pilot faculty development programs the pilot programs provided an onground understanding which will be included in devising future programs as mentioned in the strategy above 1 peer learning camaraderie providing a space for the participants either from the same institute or different ones to share their challenges as a faculty facilitated the openness for camaraderie and connect with each other as peer learners this also facilitated the process of learning by learning from each other 2 handson experience a handson experience is useful for the participants to gain insights and perspective of their peers and to reflect upon and utilise the learnings for their own teaching practices 3 contextual content contextualising the content of the program in terms of case studies referred to or examples used is a gap that needs to be filled in the further design of these programs program elements for upcoming faculty development programs the faculty development program either online or in physical mode should ensure the 3 factors to provide maximum learning output to its participants  relevance   relatability and applicability  key requirements for effective fdps ensuring that the content is relevant for the faculty of cstis is extremely important and has been a constant feedback from programs which engaged experts from management institutes the knowledge partners who will conduct further fdp for cbc and associated cstis will have to ensure that the context of examples utilised in the teaching program are from the central or state government and address the issues relevant to the public administration ecosystem similarly the teaching techniques methodology or principles taught through faculty development programs should be relatable to the participants keeping in mind their context as well as the context of their learners the faculty participating in fdp should also be able to use their learnings back at their institutes immediately after the programs ensuring an immediate and a sustained change suggested broad topics for faculty development programs online fdp level 1  fdp in physical mode level 2  a  realising the role of a facilitator b  introduction to the elements of course design from training needs analysis upto the assessment design of the course c  adult learning and learning design principles d  foundation principles such as bloom s taxonomy kolb s experiential learning cycle etc e  introduction to diverse pedagogical techniques such as case writing flipped classroom etc f  evolving ecosystem of education space with technology the advanced fdp a 34 day inperson program should build on the online fdp and take the learning experience beyond it to provide a handsonexperience to the participants the selected faculty for this program should be engaged closely and encouraged to demonstrate the skills of their role as a faculty techniques such as demo classes facilitating case teaching participating in flipped classrooms etc can be utilised in the design of the advanced level 2 faculty development program preassessment for level 1 pilot fdp preassessment for level 1 pilot fdp for a homogeneous mixture of officers from nacin tool  preassessment selfassessment for a learner 1 parameter practising adult learning principles question  how confident do you feel in practising adult learning principles in your teaching addressing the challenges of adult learning and utilising the motivations of adult learners  rating scale  a  i am not aware of the adult learning principles  score   b  i am aware of the adult learning principles but not confident in applying them for my teaching  score 1  c  i can use adult learning principles in my teaching but i am not aware of how to measure their effectiveness towards learning  score 3  d  i can use adult learning principles review consult and improvise to ensure maximum learning impact  score 5  2 parameter utilizing learning facilitation question  how confident are you about facilitating learning among your trainees the ability to facilitate practice and reflection for the learners and transfer control to the learners  rating scale  a  i cannot distinguish learning facilitation from regular teaching  score   b  i know about facilitating learning but am not equipped with knowledge of applying it in my teaching sessions  score 1  c  i can aim for facilitating learning among my trainees but i am not sure about its effect on learning  score 3  d  i can facilitate learning for my trainees and improvise based on the cohort of trainees to ensure maximum learning impact  score 5  3 parameter utilizing learning design principles question  i ensure that i plan my teaching sessions as per learning design principles being an artist creating experiences to ensure learning and citizencentric service delivery being able to prompt learners to practice what they learn and help them adapt new skills or ways of working ensures the success of training  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  4 parameter facilitating reflective learning question  i ensure reflective learning in all my teachings reflection is a necessary part of the learning cycle for engaging with theory and learning content understanding it in one s own context and determining its applicability engaging in numerous observations feedback dialogues and active experimentation activities  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  5 parameter encouraging immersive learning experiences question  i am confident in creating immersive learning experiences for my trainees creating spaces to encourage conversations and discussions around learning and create a community of practice among their learners this offers social emotional and practical support to learners for development  rating scale  a  not confident  score   b  learned but not confident  score 1  c  somewhat confident  score 3  d  completely confident  score 5  6 parameter cocreating content question  how confident do you feel in cocreating content for any training involving perspectives from relevant stakeholders cocreating content either at the stage of design or during the program through openended sessions is a way to ensure that the training is not placed out of the context of the learners  rating scale  a  not confident  score   b  learned but not confident  score 1  c  somewhat confident  score 3  d  completely confident  score 5  7 parameter enabling coaching and feedback question  i am confident in coaching my trainees and provide relevant feedback feedback is a critical factor of a training program for improving practice individual feedback based on observed behaviors challenges learners as well as guides them towards growth  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  8 parameter ensuring longterm training impact question  i aim for longterm training impact through feasible interventions post the training session keeping the focus on reinforcing learnings over time motivating learners to be invested in their learning and prompting them to practice what they have learnt at their jobs over time will reflect the impact of training and thus the effectiveness of training sessions  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  9 parameter building futuristic capabilities question  i am confident in adapting to the latest teaching methodologies and medium digital phygital of teaching upgrading one s knowledge with evolving teaching methodologies and evolving learners in the age of information  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  10 parameter developing digital comfort question  i am confident in utilising digital learning tools to ensure optimum learning through digital or phygital learning mediums adapting to the philosophy of learning from anywhere anytime empowered by digital empowerment and utilising it to the benefit of teaching  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  11 parameter transacting field experiences through academic frameworks question  how confident are you to build a course on a theme relevant for your trainees comprising of academic frameworks putting all the learnings from the field into frameworks that could be taught into a classroom thus opening new doors of opportunity for learning for the trainees as well as the world outside  rating scale  a  i like the idea and i am eager to know how to make it possible  score   b  i appreciate the idea and i have been trying to do so for some time  score 1  c  i enjoy this technique of using my field experiences to train my trainees  score 3  d  i utilise this approach confidently in all my teaching sessions  score 5  12 parameter measuring impact question  i confidently deploy techniques and tools to measure the impact of my training on trainees and their performance ensuring adequate measurement of immediate takeaway of knowledge impact on the performance of the trainees post several months of the training as well as the changes in behaviors of the trainees  rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  13 parameter staying true to the role of a trainer question  i confidently overcome challenges i face as a trainer to stay true to ensure learning for my trainees rating scale  a  not like me at all  score   b  not much like me  score 1  c  somewhat like me  score 3  d  mostly like me  score 4  e  very much like me  score 5  admin fri 12 dec 2025 559  ', 0);
